# Comments & documentation

- Comments only at file, class, function/method, and non-obvious block level. No inline
  comments restating obvious code. **All comments in English.**
- Forbidden: conversational tone, jokes, emoji, em dash (`—`), decorative banners, and
  `TODO`/`FIXME` without a ticket reference.
- Justified when: file purpose is unclear, behavior is non-obvious / has edge cases, a class
  encapsulates a non-trivial concept, or a block is surprising (workaround, ordering invariant,
  perf trick, encoded business rule).
- **JSDoc** module-level for any file with significant logic; on public/non-trivial functions
  when params/return/contract are not self-evident. Trivial private helpers do not need it.
- Do not create or extend Markdown under `docs/` or the repo root unless explicitly requested.
